# Claude Code parses `.claude/**` itself (agent + skill frontmatter, hook and pipeline
# scripts). Pin those files to LF in the WORKING TREE, not just in the repo.
#
# Why: `core.autocrlf=true` (the Windows default) stores LF but checks out CRLF, so a file's
# line endings depend on which tool last wrote it — an accident, not a decision. This is
# insurance, not a diagnosis (CRLF is not known to break the loader): it removes an arbitrary
# per-file variable, and stops a `git checkout` from silently rewriting a file whose content
# the loader caches. See `.claude/docs/agent-loading-troubleshooting.md`.
.claude/**/*.md text eol=lf
.claude/**/*.mjs text eol=lf
.claude/*.md text eol=lf
